# The server image builds two things: apps/server (Go) and apps/console (Vite).
# Everything else in this repo is context Docker packs up and ships to the
# daemon before the first instruction runs — 5.5GB of it, of which ~4.7GB is the
# Android app's node_modules and Gradle output that the image never reads.
.git
.github
**/node_modules

# The whole Android app: its own toolchain, never part of the server image.
apps/android
apps/enroll

# Built by the console stage itself. Excluded as well as cleaned, because a
# stale local dist/ shipped as a release once already: the Dockerfile now does
# `rm -rf dist` before building, and this keeps it out of the context entirely.
apps/console/dist

# Operator-facing material, not build input.
docs
deploy
qr
apk
brand
*.png
*.md
